            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0265" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89France/50: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-01-01T17:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 1,
                                1925—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1. My 614, December 30, 7 p.m. I have requested both Herriot and Clémentel to say
                    nothing about the latter’s note, and believe it may be advisable, considering
                    nature of proposal, for Department to regard it as confidential.</p>
                <p>Detailed newspaper rumor has already appeared in regard to the note, but I
                    believe that this is attributable to source which has since been stopped. I am
                    informing press correspondents that there is no new development.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
